## lever-moments

lever-moments-ask = When is a lever in balance?
lever-moments-title = The condition of a lever’s balance
lever-moments-question = A lever ruler hangs on an axis in a stand and balances by itself; the holes for the hooks are every 5 cm. We hang 100 g weights left and right at different distances from the axis, then balance them with a dynamometer. Each time we find the moment on each side: M = F·l. When is a lever in balance?
lever-moments-choices = When the moments on both sides are equal: F₁·l₁ = F₂·l₂
lever-moments-choices-2 = When the forces on both sides are the same
lever-moments-choices-3 = When the arms on both sides are the same
lever-moments-setup = A lever ruler on an axis in a stand, 100 g weights, a dynamometer
